From fab25059e5c0dbd4159b68421c984b33e3830046 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ChopGimp <mathieu.redon@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 19:15:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 103/106] ChopGimp: store rendered layer effects in XCF
 (private layer property) and seed the filters cache on load

When saving, the valid content of each layer's filters cache (layer
coordinates, effect margins included) is stored zlib-compressed as
PROP_CHOPGIMP_FX_CACHE (0x43484F50), with a SHA-256 key over the build
identity (ELF build-ids of the executable and GEGL/babl), image
precision and profile, cache format and bounds, and the whole GEGL graph
feeding the cache (operations, all properties, buffers hashed by
content, connections). Nothing is rendered at save time; size, area and
time caps apply. On load, the key is recomputed from the loaded layer
and filters and the stored pixels are seeded into the cache only if it
matches. Stock GIMP skips the unknown property; no XCF version change.

Switch: chopgimprc [xcf] fx-cache=false or CHOPGIMP_NO_XCF_FX_CACHE=1;
debug output with CHOPGIMP_FX_CACHE_DEBUG=1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
