+/* GIMP - The GNU Image Manipulation Program
+ * Copyright (C) 1995 Spencer Kimball and Peter Mattis
+ *
+ * chopgimp-fx-cache.c — ChopGimp: rendered layer effects stored in XCF
+ *
+ * Opening an image recomputes every layer's non-destructive filters
+ * ("layer styles"): this is most of the CPU cost of opening a poster
+ * with effects. When saving an XCF, the already rendered output of the
+ * filters of a layer (the content of its filters cache, see
+ * gimp_drawable_get_source_node(): a gegl:cache right after the filter
+ * stack, in layer coordinates, effect margins included) is stored as a
+ * private layer property, with a key describing everything it was
+ * computed from. When loading, if the key computed from the loaded layer
+ * and filters is the same, the stored pixels are put in the layer's
+ * filters cache, which is then valid: nothing is recomputed until the
+ * layer or its filters change, which invalidates the cache as usual.
+ *
+ * - Saving never renders: only the regions of the cache which are valid
+ *   are stored, and only for layers above a size threshold, within a
+ *   per-layer size cap and a per-save time budget.
+ * - The key (SHA-256) covers: a build identity (ELF build-ids of the
+ *   ChopGimp executable and of the loaded GEGL/babl libraries and
+ *   modules, plus their versions), the image precision, base type and
+ *   color profile, the cache's pixel format and bounding box, and the
+ *   whole GEGL graph feeding the cache: every node's operation, all of
+ *   its properties (layer pixels and any other buffer hashed by
+ *   content, colors, paths, curves, GimpConfig objects serialized),
+ *   and how the nodes are connected — so filter order, visibility,
+ *   opacity, blend mode, region, clip and mask are included. A property
+ *   which cannot be described reliably makes the layer ineligible.
+ *   Doubles are hashed with the float precision XCF stores filter
+ *   arguments with, unless "fx-cache-strict" is set.
+ * - Anything unexpected (parse error, mismatch, different format or
+ *   bounding box) ignores the stored data: rendering is never altered.
+ * - Stock GIMP skips unknown properties (xcf_skip_unknown_prop()) and
+ *   drops them when saving: no XCF version change.
+ *
+ * Settings (${gimp_dir}/chopgimprc, group [xcf]):
+ *   fx-cache=false               neither write nor read
+ *   fx-cache-strict=true         hash doubles exactly
+ *   fx-cache-min-pixels=65536    smallest cached area stored per layer
+ *   fx-cache-max-mb=256          largest uncompressed data per layer
+ *   fx-cache-save-budget-ms=3000 time spent per save
+ *   fx-cache-zlib-level=1
+ * Environment: CHOPGIMP_NO_XCF_FX_CACHE=1 disables it,
+ * CHOPGIMP_FX_CACHE_DEBUG=1 prints what is stored, seeded or rejected.
+ *
+ * This program is free software: you can redistribute it and/or modify
+ * it under the terms of the GNU General Public License as published by
+ * the Free Software Foundation; either version 3 of the License, or
+ * (at your option) any later version.
+ *
+ * This program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful,
+ * but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of
